=== PARITY (vs web EnergyFlowAnimatedWidget.tsx — distinct from sibling EnergyFlowWidget) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (EnergyFlowAnimatedSource → …Model):
    useVehicles, useVehicleState(id, refetchInterval 5s), useTranslation. The production app wires
    the source over the KMP VehiclesStore (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>), resolving the
    selected vehicle the way the web's `vehicleId ?? vehicles[0].id` does; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection → EnergyFlowAnimatedBuilder.buildProjection is a 1:1 port of the web memoized nodes/arrows.
    The animated widget's distinguishing behaviours are ALL reproduced + unit-asserted:
      • ±0.5 kW drive dead-band (web `power > 0.5` / `power < -0.5`, NOT 0) — drive shows Drive/Regen/Idle.
      • nodes ALWAYS all three: battery(left,%), drive(right,kW@1 or dash), charger(top,kW@0 or dash)
        — the charger is present even when unplugged (web nodes memo is unconditional), unlike the sibling.
      • arrows ALWAYS all three: battery→drive(cyan), drive→battery(emerald), charger→battery(amber);
        inactive arrows carry value 0 (minimal stroke, no marching dash).
      • node glyphs are UNCOLORED (web icons carry no Tailwind color → inherit --text-primary).
    Stroke ∝ magnitude (1..4); compact keeps the 3 largest. Verified by EXECUTED XCTest (33/33) below.
  Compact (web `CompactView`, size.cols < 2) → EnergyFlowAnimatedCompactView: hero `{batteryLevel}%`
    above ordered active chips (charging→Plug/amber, consuming→Zap/cyan, regen→Battery/emerald, each at
    1 decimal kW), else "Idle". Surface picks CompactView for cols<2, the full diagram otherwise.
  Composition → glass widget shell (Zap→`bolt.fill` cyan-400 + "Energy Flow" title + freshness chip +
    refresh + optional Open) · EnergyFlowAnimatedDiagram (Canvas-stroked arrows with marching-dash flow +
    node circles: SF Symbol + live value + label outside the ring). Recharts→none / Leaflet→none.
    Web SVG <line>/<circle>/<foreignObject> → Canvas + positioned SwiftUI views (crisp symbols +
    numericText value). lucide→SF: Zap→bolt.fill, Battery→battery.100percent, Plug→powerplug.fill.
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No energy data available", web
    `state?…:EmptyState`) · error (Retry) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached + chip + banner) ·
    content (compact or diagram). Model phase resolution keeps cached content visible behind
    refresh/errors (web shell behaviour). The web shell only passes `isError` (freshness), so the
    prompt-required hard-error state (no cache) renders a Retry affordance, matching the 0046 precedent.
  i18n → all 7 source keys (namespace "dashboard": widget.energyFlowAnimated.{title,battery,drive,regen,
    idle,charger,noData}) resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback.
